{"base_rate":0.4583883751651255,"brier":0.12000964332893,"bss":0.5166134385323681,"bss_hi":0.5908115243933697,"bss_lo":0.4354818089802302,"chart":{"base":[656.4,48.4],"fp":[248.2,322.2],"lead":"62,271.9 272,246.2 482,198.8 692,141.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.52 — higher than 93% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +11pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 82% of cities","rel":"promised 4% → rained 8%; promised 96% → rained 87%"},"rel":"84.5,430.4 377,302.5 666.5,90.5"},"country":"EE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07898282694848087,"ess":398.7025833512725,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tallinn</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tallinn rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>93%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTALLINN, 9.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.52, ranked 15 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(6&ndash;43) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>214</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>89</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>65%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>93%</b></td><td class='num'>229</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tallinn</b> <span class=\"muted\">Estonia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.52</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>6&ndash;43\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tallinn &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tallinn\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%